---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Callout } from "astro-ink";
---
<Base title="Callout">
  <div class="docs-page">
    <h1>Callout</h1>
    <p class="docs-lede">
      A semantic side note: info, success, warning, danger. The accent edge
      carries meaning, never decoration.
    </p>

    <h2>Example</h2>
    <div class="docs-example" style="display: grid;">
      <span class="docs-example-label" aria-hidden="true">Example</span>
      <Callout title="Deprecation notice" variant="warning">
        The legacy export ends in December. Migrate to the workspace layout.
      </Callout>
    </div>
    <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;Callout title="Deprecation notice" variant="warning"&gt;
  The legacy export ends in December.
&lt;/Callout&gt;</code></pre>

    <h2>Props</h2>
    <table class="docs-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Prop</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>variant</code></td><td><code>info | success | warning | danger</code></td><td><code>info</code></td><td>Also colors the edge.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>style</code></td><td><code>tint | filled</code></td><td><code>tint</code></td><td>Filled uses white text on the semantic color (AA).</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>title</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>-</td><td>Becomes the region label.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <ul class="docs-list">
      <li>Renders a labeled <code>section</code> (region landmark).</li>
      <li>The edge color always pairs with the title text: never color alone.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
